<title>FRANCE: French call money lowered 1/16 percentage point.</title>
<headline>French call money lowered 1/16 percentage point.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>- French call money was lowered to 3 1/8 1/4 from 3 3/16 5/16 percent yesterday, traders said.</p>
<p>The lowering of the French overnight rate, seen as a semi-official interest rate, follows a five basis point cut in the intervention rate on Thursday to 3.10 percent.</p>
<p>The intervention rate sets the floor for French money market rates.</p>
<p>Call money was last cut on December 18, the day after the intervention rate was cut to 3.15 percent from 3.20 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
